course: dictionary
lesson: 4679
title: Holstein, a cow and a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Holstein is a word with two meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it and ask: is this about animals on a farm, or about a place? «Many cow breeds are brown, red or black; only some dairy breeds such as the Holstein are black and white.» Here Holstein is a kind of cow, because it sits in a list of cow breeds and is linked to colour and patterns.
explain: A Holstein is a large black-and-white dairy cow, famous for giving a lot of milk. In the UK you may also hear it called a Friesian, or Holstein-Friesian. These are different names for the same cow. Dairy means milk: a dairy cow is kept for its milk.
explain: Holstein can also be a name for a place. Holstein is a region in northern Germany, and it is part of Schleswig-Holstein. If the sentence talks about travelling, maps or towns, think about the place. Always check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A Holstein is a breed of large black-and-white dairy cow.
fact: Holsteins are famous for giving a lot of milk.
fact: The classic cartoon cow with black and white patches is a Holstein.
fact: Holsteins are the most common dairy cows in the USA, Canada, the UK, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Holstein is also a region in northern Germany, part of Schleswig-Holstein.
exercise: «Only some dairy breeds such as the Holstein are black and white.» What is a Holstein? | A breed of sheep kept for wool | A kind of cheese | A brown and red horse | *A large black-and-white dairy cow
exercise: Ella's mum says, «We drove through Holstein in northern Germany.» What does Holstein mean here? | A farm shop | *A region in northern Germany | A kind of milk | A black-and-white cow
exercise: «Each cow's pattern is unique like a fingerprint.» What does unique mean? | Spotted | Very common | *One of a kind, different from all others | Painted
test: «In the UK, Holstein cows are often called Friesians.» What does this tell you? | *Friesian is another name for the Holstein cow | Holsteins live only in Germany | Friesians are horses | Friesians are a kind of sheep
test: What does dairy mean in the phrase «dairy breeds»? | *Kept for their milk | Used for riding | Kept for their wool | Kept as pets
exam: Which sentence uses Holstein as a place, not a cow? | *Our train passed through Holstein on the way north. | Our class read about the Holstein cow's milk. | Our cow was a Holstein with black patches. | The Holstein gave ten litres of milk today.
